 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259057 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259057 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259057 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186258912 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259057 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0d42c87d-8e24-585c-849a-f00efbd599ce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259176 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186257118 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259176 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186257483 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259176 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186258664 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259176 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186258717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259176 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186258981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259176 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259176 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259176 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186258664 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259176 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "514ff102-c238-5181-bd9a-4ee63292ed41" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259641 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259057 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259641 #edb/ref 1069 "q-124262" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259641 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259641 #edb/ref 1071 "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=au+v,\\,y=bu+cv\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 9 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259641 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "18f13e13-3246-593c-9da3-b608f58de1b5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259641 #edb/ref 1074 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 9 & 3\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2u+v \\\\ 9u+3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2u+v \\\\ 9u+3v\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=-2u+v,\\,y=9u+3v\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-2+9+3=10.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259642 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259176 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259642 #edb/ref 1069 "q-124263" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259642 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259642 #edb/ref 1071 "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=4u+av-2,\\,y=bu+cv-3\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 9 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259642 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "569ad093-da2b-5144-992e-0f84b411665b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259642 #edb/ref 1074 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 9 & 5\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4u-v \\\\ 9u+5v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4u-v-2 \\\\ 9u+5v-3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=4u+(-1)v-2,\\,y=9u+5v-3\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-1+9+5=13.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
